{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0472c816e5e1567a64c9fb5f528503717900713ac1dc0a034c90818a04b512ad","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1e43e00cfa70ba86de731938ff61d31574ab436ebab594dd1d59dfd70f4fbb64","slc_3bfb30e7746e800222ff191bbdd6b148e81cb85a6bf5dc6be4f23aa11018436b"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"The repo ships a TypeScript CLI/orchestrator core, a Rust ratatui TUI, a Tauri desktop GUI (React + Vite frontend, Rust backend), and a shared Rust crate harness-data that reads ~/.relay/ for both dashboards.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_071215cf671c5309749e756f9ccd993eacac7b4dfb85659f2065c6de3a0323a5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1ac94267bf8f5d6c515894c32d0c60a98be341720622e93941a680aa26e3dfa4","slc_ab3f9a4a32c5dfa71d723e09d6dee4ac48bd10000595cb3327ba922aa7708895"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"The two CLI adapters (claude, codex) accept any endpoint speaking their wire protocol, so OpenAI- or Anthropic-compatible HTTP providers work by setting base-URL and key env vars; named profiles reference env-var names rather than storing secrets.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_267e21a505cb5abef02ee8f841ccdfb8a8740d84c77d14dce9e13e08312c6011","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e260d7d34e2fb2860f46cd6883e717c715cee5ec766b6ddcbd8cacc0be1c7500"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"With GITHUB_TOKEN set, a background PR watcher polls every 30 seconds; CI failures and changes-requested reviews automatically become follow-up tickets via the scheduler's dynamic enqueue.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_26d5d598d767b361e06a00c4ceb4a4246722b25a63f3688ea0ab29cb9a2182da","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b45ee136b72c5921cb250da5e7bf4adc1944da6a07347c76a5853e3d680d2a4d","slc_c26831aa2836854d46ba8f9c8354350cf2090a17e9de8bbb6fad707334127cdf"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"GitHub integration requires GITHUB_TOKEN (with project scope for Projects v2 sync) and Linear integration uses LINEAR_API_KEY or COMPOSIO_API_KEY; the CLI needs Node >= 20 and pnpm to build from source.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_31076e71e94b1e08a6eb7ad67300cbe2a6eaa18f2efd1c63b8368ee88bfd7736","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_01c05fbb13c71ce6ce6327f3f5ef5824db7f5d80260523d9f163d2d9de24ef5d","slc_064b6cc7d22e9ffd487ffa5e19ba50f5637bdc653be14b99ffdb9ce28a152467","slc_52e470b474e9eebbdadd84a215db1a18ab404699369ce732bdf94c82f91384fd","slc_a33c47bf03984269f75f9e6f3cc18a2d3a97ada0d9ec32594984388cfab79d0f","slc_ee3fc82a8c8ef6a391fbb95d3c80a53c58e848b547942130b2c0af1c59a0ae01"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"Relay exposes an MCP server to Claude and Codex with harness tools (e.g. harness_approve_plan, harness_dispatch), channel tools (channel_create, channel_record_decision, channel_handoff_finalize), and crosslink tools (crosslink_discover/send/poll); rly inspect-mcp lists the live set.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_37125d3f7f55a01e834bc4060e438fa241e1061f36211dead2e18e59fafa2ecd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_362f08db976946f0f6a7e1ad3c1b4078f12565385b5a8886f3a14761dd9b8088"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"Cross-repo agents discover each other via heartbeat files under ~/.relay/crosslink/sessions/ and exchange messages directly through the crosslink MCP tools.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_44a45558cbb503f5be92c798957d58923e76e1d616be147648a8dc056b074539","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d628a0a99e5c8a027d908590b94fd1e244e330a3589ae73625635d5d03bf7647"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"Requests are classified into complexity tiers (trivial, bugfix, feature_small, feature_large, architectural, multi_repo); feature_large and above require user approval via MCP, while trivial/bugfix use heuristic matching.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4aefb87951f21dc0d7829388b0bacb848c124ea3a88729e01b3c94d880463286","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5f0d8ebe2592a69379e2d9c0f413583a6f10870c1077b9eb3069c8d7c28d58c1"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"The project is explicitly beta, pre-v1: APIs, CLI flags, ~/.relay file layouts, and GUI surfaces may change between releases, and users are asked to file issues with reproductions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6c0e75c44ada0711b0785cdbf0982f0742b6510d69494a609c4d2a07e4ae2185","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0566869aeb8e30efa60ff91fe6e9908241345aaccaa5dd13f61ac3b9b17397b4","slc_59ddfe1af1587c7c9f4bb62b3eaff34509212cf8849ea9b277f4178dbe0b8be2","slc_80d28fc80bc3334c39a9b871cc19c4c71a1493d22831951eedd44878f41ce88e"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"Autonomous runs are bounded by wall-clock hours, a token budget, and a STOP-file kill switch, and verification commands run against an allowlist rather than being shelled blindly.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_722c218579a7fae6055f0a56b0287593bb14940c3b87f2abc5624c67f91bf681","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7e57ce6acf4a4f10e307c5ad3d0ce5dc932f27bbe4637ae9a97ad69716fb2088"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"Relay converts a sentence, GitHub issue URL, or Linear ticket into a running plan: classify, plan, decompose into a ticket DAG, dispatch to Claude or Codex agents, verify, open a PR, and track until merged.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7eec4fa07472284f1265b10901b07d69ce060728dedf449da3addc2963566a54","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_186fd6ab4a3ec245210c0ca18e4c87b8a29fa54c57944bc6d7972ffae22a7d2e"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"Documented limits: cross-platform spawn is lightly tested off macOS, and cost guardrails (per-run dollar/token budget caps) are not yet implemented, though per-session context-window telemetry ships in v0.7.x.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8434eeb3dc3d82771621c0156c261865f957029e6da3e11b503134ad252fd9fc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1b563938ca49f654a34d1ad279e88879dbf3df8b0b45bbae2c8f1fb4723404e8","slc_c24ee579c8b6ace5e7ac23719e25512470b2354de15b034670bb5838145a7e1e","slc_e1de3be5cb9d664100ac68841d97d54b9ba0814e524490165e5c008c26153422"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"Cross-repo work is designed to go through the primary repo's tools rather than file reads: quick questions use crosslink_send, longer tasks are tickets with assignedAlias routing, and the primary agent is told not to grep or edit associated repos directly.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8d50777bac5605ed996fa4541a6b0736ec19d107bbfb7bef67216446e9acbed2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ea9f4eee4222e71156466095a550778ec1f84b48f804d4e0bb11f0a58718b771"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"The pipeline runs classifier → planner (design doc if architectural) → decomposer into a dependency-DAG of tickets → scheduler running tickets in parallel capped by max-concurrency, then implement/verify/retry until a PR opens.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9bde2121bbb7063907cb602e8362fcfb84dbd4650a020f51d9f1cf475f5ac488","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7d4a181e98ce0ee57eb64b4e44569af9e756ada45d5485d499faf29965c801f8","slc_b61c0c7c5ade59149c3c3be8211b56bcc8ca727a0c764a6966169255dcbc4f6d"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"Verification runs through an Executor abstraction whose only shipping implementation is LocalChildProcessExecutor; a pod-based executor was prototyped and removed, and a Postgres HarnessStore backend is stubbed but not wired (HARNESS_STORE=postgres falls back to files).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9e88a85f75c1e3eb2b609655ca96eca15b981755966689e36aaae5073562360a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"jcast90/relay@7bd5a2f6a13c snapshot eb9f73091bfb91b5","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8e75185f4a6a11bcdfffd509d0a4859c1b8c58445c82c4cd6abfd6ba9d3cc263","slc_9efe2747dad103161c23224c2021912513df1d4260db4ad0db5208fd2aa71c81","slc_f4133bc1b1f0ee011ac0034650857e0560ad9202036eb3d6993da20d26323c40"],"source_ids":["src_9f143dfb8d245ea4a08a657404b21094"],"text":"Issue-tracker and SCM integrations build on Composio's @aoagents/ao-core leaf plugins, and Relay exports a HarnessChannelNotifier so it can act as a notifier plugin for Composio's ao orchestrator.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:07:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_81731347403d4438890db0ff3817d67a"}
